# Copy this file to ".env", fill in your keys, then restart the Expo server
# (`npx expo start --clear`) — keys are read at build time, so a running server
# will not pick up edits to this file.
#
# The app only ever shows real API data. Without a key the Explore and Map
# screens say so instead of inventing houses.
#
# NOTE: anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is embedded in the JS bundle and is
# readable by anyone who installs the app. That is fine for a personal build,
# but do not ship these keys in a public release.

# ── RentCast (REQUIRED) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Finds the houses around you, and supplies beds/baths/sqft/year built/last
# sale/owner names. Also provides one of the two current-value estimates.
# Sign up: https://www.rentcast.io/api
# Create a key: https://app.rentcast.io/app/api
#
# Heads up: the free Developer plan includes only 50 requests per month. The
# app spends one per ~40m you walk, plus one more each time you tap a house
# for its value estimate. See README for how to stretch it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RENTCAST_API_KEY=

# ── Zillow via RapidAPI (OPTIONAL) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Adds Zillow's Zestimate alongside RentCast's estimate when you tap a house.
# Not used to find houses — that's RentCast's job.
# Subscribe to zillow-com1: https://rapidapi.com/apimaker/api/zillow-com1
#
# This is a third-party scraper of Zillow, not an official API. It is ToS-gray
# and can break without notice. Leave blank to skip Zestimates entirely.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RAPIDAPI_KEY=
